<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tajura</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tajoura</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tajura is a coastal town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a>, just east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripoli">Tripoli</a>. In the mid-16th century it served as a base for the Ottoman corsair <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turgut-reis">Turgut Reis</a> and other opponents of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-hospitaller">Knights Hospitaller</a>, who then held Tripoli. From there the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> prepared the siege that took Tripoli from the knights in 1551.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tajura.jpg" alt="Tajura" width="320" height="175" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown (offered by TCI, Touring Club Italiano) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tagiura_map.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
